<title>USA: US Senate panel to hold fast track trade hearing.</title>
<headline>US Senate panel to hold fast track trade hearing.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate Finance Committee said on Thursday it will hold a hearing June 3 on the need for renewal of the president's &quot;fast track&quot; trade negotiating authority.</p>
<p>U.S. Trade Representative Charlene Barshefsky is scheduled to testify at the hearing, which begins at 1000 EDT/1400 GMT.</p>
<p>Granting fast track authority would allow the president to negotiate international trade agreements that Congress then would either have to approve or reject without amendments.</p>
</text>
